202:Inside the Target Building
203:Let's first consider where the victims might be hidden. It's likely to be in buildings that are difficult to search thoroughly.
204:This city seems pretty safe. If you know your way around, it shouldn't be hard to find places that fit the bill.
205:That's true, nyaa! Though I can't guarantee we'll find your friend, let's at least try, nyaa!
206:You're doing us a great favor already. It turns out we really do need to rely on the help of locals for something like this.
207:So is Sakura reaching out to people she knows who might come help, nyaa?
208:It just happens that the two people she is contacting came to One Han City from the same place as us at the same time. We didn't travel together.
209:Yes, but they didn't pick up my call, so I sent them a message explaining the situation.
210:Our relationship isn't really one of companionship, so we shouldn't rely on them too much.
212:Fair point. Senpai is one grade ahead of me, has red hair, and was wearing our school's uniform when he came here.
213:Hmm, there are also high school students with red hair in One Han City, nyaa. Any other quirks or traits I should know about, nyaa?
214:He even helped me, someone who was basically a stranger to him. He's just too kind.
215:You're correct about him being an incredibly kind person, but that often leads him to act way too recklessly.
217:R-Really tight...?!
218:N-Not really. He saved me, so I really want to repay him...
219:Oh? Ichihime, and two unfamiliar faces? Why are you all in such a hurry? Did something happen?
220:Ah!
222:Oh, this is Fu Ji, and she owns a mahjong dojo called Luck and Fortune.
224:Hi! Since fate brought us together, why not swing by my place? A round of mahjong will bring good luck and keep misfortune at bay. What do you say?
225:S-Sorry... we're in the middle of something urgent right now. We'll definitely come when we are free.
226:Well, I bet my situation is more urgent than yours. Do any of you have a phone on you?
227:Hmph... I don't know which fool decided to kidnap me, but they did! First things first, I need to call the police, and then I'll settle the score.
228:I could have escaped earlier, but I decided to play along because I was worried there would be other victims.
231:To be precise, just as I was starting to think of a plan, that person started making a fuss, which drew the kidnappers' attention. I figured it was the perfect chance and slipped out.
232:The person she mentioned is gotta be Shirou. He was probably taken to the same place as Fu Ji after he was kidnapped.
233:Oh, so that guy's name is Shirou. Well, it's thanks to him that I could escape without a hitch.
234:But you can stop stressing about him getting hurt. Other than being locked up for a few days, I came out just fine.
235:They didn't lay a finger on me. Honestly, they were so polite that it wouldn't have surprised me if they'd said something like, "Please enjoy your stay here for a while."
236:Yeah, and I got the feeling that they also wanted to avoid using violence if they could.
237:But instead of calling them kind, I think they were just trying to avoid piling on more crimes. I mean, can you really call a kidnapper "kind"?
238:Well, since I stumbled into something like this, I figured I might as well dig up some info about the kidnappers and report them to the police for a reward. But unfortunately, after watching them for so long, I didn't find anything useful.
241:We're racing against time now. If we rush over now, we might still find the kidnappers and Shirou there.
242:B-But what can we do when we get there? The kidnappers will just lock us up if they are still there. That would be the end of us, nyaa!
243:Don't worry, I won't let anything happen to us.
245:Seems the kidnappers moved immediately after realizing I had escaped. Tsk, they're really cunning.
246:It's a shame that the kidnappers managed to slip away, but finding where they held their victims this quickly is already a big step forward.
251:Sure.
252:With your knowledge of this city, we'll have a greater chance of finding Shirou if we can get more people to help us.
253:But didn't you just say that there were only three of you...?
254:By the way, what's this Shirou Emiya guy like, nyaa?
